      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen vacancies provide stronger anchoring sites for Pt.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stronger Pt anchoring reduces Pt sintering during prolonged exposure to harsh exhaust conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced Pt sintering decreases catalyst deactivation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimized Pt/Ce1-xZrxO2 will have higher oxidation-reaction turnover frequencies than Pt/CeO2 under identical conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimized Pt/Ce1-xZrxO2 will retain activity better than Pt/CeO2 during extended thermal redox cycling.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The activity and durability improvements will persist at lower Pt loadings, thereby reducing platinum-group-metal consumption.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Zr fraction of approximately x = 0.1-0.2 is an optimal range for the proposed improvements.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr fractions outside the proposed optimal range may produce suboptimal oxygen-vacancy concentrations and compromise stability.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternating oxidizing and reducing environments at 350-700°C are representative of automotive exhaust redox cycling for purposes of the test.",
